= Name

==
The name of the society shall be *Warwick Students’ Union NAME OF SOCIETY*.


= Aims and Objectives

==
The Society shall have a written statement of aims and objectives providing a clear understanding of the society. This shall be subject to review annually by the *SOCIETY NAME* Executive Committee.

==
The society aims and objectives shall be:
- Aims of Society 1  
- Aims of Society 2  
- Objectives of Society 1  
- Objectives of Society 2  

==
The Society, its Executives, its funds and all its activities shall be subject to the provisions of the By-Laws, Regulations and Policy of the University of Warwick Students’ Union.

==
The Society shall be subject to a disciplinary code as laid down and administered by the Students’ Union.

==
Any alterations to the Society Constitution must be ratified by the Societies Forum. A provisional copy must be sent to the Vice President for Societies for approval before the new constitution may take effect.

==
If the Society has issues arising not mentioned in a personalised Constitution, then this document will become the default. Any issues may be dealt with by contacting your Societies Coordinator.

= Memberships

==
Membership of the Society shall be open to all full, associate and honorary members of the Students’ Union upon payment of the required Societies Federation subscription.

==
Memberships of the Society are to be renewed in the September of every academic year.

==
Only standard members of the society shall be entitled to vote in elections, provided they have joined the society and paid the appropriate subscription fee no less than three days before the election takes place.

==
The following shall not be entitled to hold the office of an Executive position in the society:
- An Associate or Honorary member of the Students’ Union or Societies Federation  
- Any person who has received payment for the provision of services to the society (not including reimbursement of personal expenditure on behalf of the society)

==
The Society must have a minimum of 30 members by the sixth week of term one. If the minimum membership is not met, a meeting with the Society and their Societies Coordinator will be scheduled to discuss the future of the Society.

= Executive Committee

==
The Society’s Executive Committee shall be made up of at least three *Core Roles* who shall be the President/Chair, the Welfare Officer and the Treasurer.

==
The Executive Committee must also ensure that they include an officer responsible for each of the *Core Responsibilities*. These responsibilities may be put under the remit of other committee members’ roles (unlike the Core Officers) and do not need to be separate officers. However, they must be specified in the Constitution. The Core Responsibilities are:
=== Equality and Diversity  
=== Safety  
=== Secretary  

==
The Executive Committee shall be responsible for the day-to-day running of the society and may decide upon any matter that has not yet been decided upon by the General Meeting. The Executive Committee shall further be responsible for:
- Organising the activities of the Society in such a way as to include the greatest possible number of Society members  
- Managing the expenditure of the Society’s funds in a responsible fashion and in line with the aims, objectives and planned activities of the Society, whilst adhering to the SU’s financial regulations  
- Formulating and submitting an annual bid for funds from Student Activities prior to any specified deadline, which shall include a statement of activities and objectives for the coming year and detailed justification of the figures contained in the bid  
- Formulating and submitting any additional bids for funds from the SU Societies Forum or groups within the Students’ Union  
- Assisting any review of the Society’s activities and use of funds carried out by a standing committee or group of the Students’ Union that has granted funds to the Society  
- Upholding the Constitution of the Society and ensuring that its aims and objectives reflect the Society’s activities  
- Ensuring that all society activity abides by the By-laws, regulations and policy of Warwick SU  
- Executive Committee members must attend assigned training to ensure they are equipped to organise the Society  

== Core Officers

=== General Core Officer Duties
- To attend the Society’s Annual General Meeting  
- To attend Societies Council and complete mandatory training sessions/courses  

=== President/Chair/Club Captain
- The President/Chair/Captain should organise and oversee the running of the Society  
- he President/Chair/Captain should chair committee meetings  

=== Treasurer
- The Treasurer should be responsible for the finances of the Society  
- The Treasurer should maintain an up-to-date record of their group account in addition to the record kept by the SU finance office  
- All funds should be held and processed through the group’s Students’ Union bank account. No money should be held in personal bank accounts  
- The Treasurer should submit grant funding applications  

=== Welfare Officer
- The Welfare Officer should be responsible for signposting Society members to the University’s and SU’s support services when a welfare issue arises  
- The Welfare Officer should make it known among Society members that they can come to them for initial support, with the understanding that support will primarily take the form of signposting (not advice)  

