= Meetings

==
The Executive must meet at least three times per term to ensure the Society is operated to a high standard.

==
The Society Executive shall call at least one General Meeting per year for the purposes of discussing plans and activities for the coming year. This must be held by Week 10, Term 2. This GM may also be used to hold Society Officer elections.

==
The Society Executive shall give at least seven days’ notice of any General Meeting to all members via Society email, and such notice shall include details of any elections to be held.

==
The Executive shall call further meetings either at its own initiative, at the request of 10% of the membership, or at the request of the Vice President for Societies.

= Elections

==
Elections shall be held online or at a quorate general meeting in line with By-Law 10 Appendix D.

==
Votes will be counted using a First Past The Post/Single Transferrable Vote electoral system.

==
Any amendments to the constitution must be made by the end of Term 3.

==
The renewed Constitution, with up-to-date signatures, must be sent to the Societies Coordinator before the end of Term 3.